# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the QML UI tests.
#
# Qt's QMutex uses a raw futex() syscall on Linux instead of
# pthread_mutex_lock/unlock, and the Qt build under test is not itself
# sanitizer-instrumented, so TSan cannot see the happens-before edges Qt
# establishes internally when it marshals data across threads. Every
# suppression below is for a race entirely inside Qt/glib/libstdc++
# runtime code (never inside our own wisdom:: or GameModel/ChessEngine
# frames), reached only because our code is what triggers the underlying
# cross-thread signal/slot delivery or thread start/stop.

# Qt copies and later destroys a std::function argument (the periodic-
# search notifier from GameModel::buildNotifier()) through QMetaType when
# marshaling GameModel::engineConfigChanged(...) across the queued
# connection to ChessEngine::updateConfig(). Seen as an operator
# delete/delete[] race inside QtPrivate::QMetaTypeForType<...>::getDtor()/
# getCopyCtr(), triggered from GameModel::updateEngineConfig()
# (game_model.cpp:393). Observed in wisdom-chess-qml-application-test and
# wisdom-chess-qml-dialogs-test.
race:QMetaType

# Qt's glib-based event dispatcher wakes another thread's event loop by
# writing to an eventfd; the write/read pair is only a wakeup signal, and
# the actual cross-thread hand-off is protected by the same uninstrumented
# Qt locking as above. Seen from GameModel::updateEngineConfig() and
# GameModel::stopEngineThread() starting/stopping the engine thread, with
# the racing write()/eventfd() calls inside libglib-2.0.so.0.
race:eventfd

# QtQuick's internal QThreadPool ('Thread (pooled)') touches Qt's
# implicitly-shared container refcounting (QArrayData::allocate, then a
# memmove inside libQt6Core.so.6) from more than one pooled worker thread
# at once. Entirely inside Qt's own container implementation; our code
# only triggers it indirectly via a UI click
# (wisdom::ui::test::Application::clickItem() opening a menu/starting a
# game). Observed in wisdom-chess-qml-dialogs-test and
# wisdom-chess-qml-mobile-test.
race:QArrayData
